<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - SAFRICA MAY M3 MONEY SUPPLY UP 15.40 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SAFRICA MAY M3 MONEY SUPPLY UP 15.40 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 15.40 percent in May, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>April M3 growth was left unchanged at 15.44 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 16.57 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 17.40 percent in April.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast M3 year-on-year growth of 15.19 percent, while private credit was seen expanding 16.56 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>May 1997 preliminary M3 growth -- 15.40 percent</p>
<p>May 1997 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 16.57</p>
<p>percent</p>
